<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia's Mulialand says 1996 net up.</title>
<headline>Indonesia's Mulialand says 1996 net up.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian property firm PT Mulialand said on Thursday it booked a net profit of 142.8 billion rupiah in 1996 against 92.8 billion rupiah in the previous year.</p>
<p>In early March, Mulialand's president director was quoted by a Jakarta newspaper as saying the company estimated its net profit would be 142 billion rupiah in 1996.</p>
<p>He also said the firm expected to book a net profit of 165 billion rupiah and 200 billion rupiah in 1997 and 1998 respectively.  </p>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>( in billion rupiah unless stated )</p>
<p>    Net profit			 142.8    vs    92.8</p>
<p>    Revenues			   555.4    vs   463.9</p>
<p>    Gross profit		     286.1    vs   241.3</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 259.0    vs   225.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   180.9    vs   168.3</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (in rph)    334    vs     245</p>
<p>    Retained earnings		305.1    vs   185.0</p>
<p>Note : The results were audited. PT Mulialand is a Jakarta-based firm which develops and operates office buildings.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
